            "advisory": "A vulnerability in Gunicorn allowed the TolerateDangerousFraming setting to process conflicting headers (Transfer-Encoding and Content-Length) and dangerous characters in HTTP header fields. This could lead to HTTP request smuggling and header injection attacks. The issue was resolved by removing this setting and enforcing stricter header validation. \r\nNote: It happens due to an incomplete fix for CVE-2024-1135.",
